ifconfig — show the current network interface config
======================================================

Minimal read-only network diagnostic — the classic "what IP
did I get?" command. Calls `inet_get_ip_config` and renders
the three fields in the familiar dotted-quad form.

Slix has exactly one logical interface right now (the virtio
nic), so there's no interface name to iterate or pass. A
future multi-NIC build would turn this into `ifconfig <ifname>`
with a per-interface table.

Output shape is three lines: `ip:`, `mask:`, `gateway:`, each
followed by the dotted-quad. Pairs naturally with `dhclient` —
dhclient sets the lease, ifconfig shows what's installed.

    module oskit.bin.ifconfig

    import oskit.ulib.{puts, exit, exit_with}
    import oskit.net.inet_get_ip_config
    import std.net.ipv4_octet


    print_udec(v: int)
        if v >= 10
            print_udec(v / 10)
        var b: [1]byte
        b[0] = byte('0' + (v % 10))
        puts(string(&b[0], 1))


    print_ipv4(ip: u32)
        print_udec(ipv4_octet(ip, 0))
        puts(".")
        print_udec(ipv4_octet(ip, 1))
        puts(".")
        print_udec(ipv4_octet(ip, 2))
        puts(".")
        print_udec(ipv4_octet(ip, 3))


    main(argv: []string)
        var ip: u32 = u32(0)
        var mask: u32 = u32(0)
        var gw: u32 = u32(0)
        if inet_get_ip_config(&ip, &mask, &gw) < 0
            puts("ifconfig: inet_get_ip_config failed\n")
            exit_with(1)
            return
        puts("ip:      ")
        print_ipv4(ip)
        puts("\n")
        puts("mask:    ")
        print_ipv4(mask)
        puts("\n")
        puts("gateway: ")
        print_ipv4(gw)
        puts("\n")
        exit()
